[68.395343, "o", "nf-2.0             \u001b[158C                                          \r\nSuggests: postgresql-doc                                           \u001b[167C                                 \r\nDownload-Size: 72.2 kB                                             \u001b[167C                                 \r\nAPT-Manual-Installed: yes                                              \u001b[C            \u001b[C                  \u001b[C                 \u001b[C                  \u001b[C                 \u001b[C                  \u001b[C                   \u001b[C                  \u001b[C                                                  \r\nAPT-Sources: https://apt\u001b[Cpostgresql.org/pub/repos/apt\u001b[Cjammy-pgdg/main amd64 Packages                                                    \u001b[C                                                   \r\nDescription: object-relational SQL database\u001b[C(supported version)                                       \u001b[C  \u001b[C                           \u001b[C  \u001b[C                                                   \u001b[46C                                 \r\n This metapackage\u001b[Calways depends on the\u001b[Ccurrently \u001b[Cupported\u001b[CPostgreSQL                                                                \r\n database server\u001b[Cversion\u001b[C It also\u001b[Coffers to\u001b[Cautomatically upgrade the                                                                 \u001b[100C                                 \r\n \"main\" database\u001b[Ccluster to the lastest\u001b[Csupported major version.            \u001b[C        \u001b[C            \u001b[128C                                 \r\n .                                                                          \u001b[C        \u001b[C          \u001b[C      \u001b[122C                                          \r\n PostgreSQL is a\u001b[Cfully\u001b[Cfeatured object-relational database management                                                                 \u001b[100C                                 \r\n system.\u001b[C It supports\u001b[Ca large part\u001b[Cof the\u001b[CSQL\u001b[Cstandard and is\u001b[Cdesigned                                                                \r\n to be extensible\u001b[Cby users\u001b[Cin many\u001b[Caspects.\u001b[2CSome of\u001b[Cth\u001b[C features are:                                                                \u001b[100C                                 \r\n ACID transactions, foreign keys,\u001b[Cviews, sequences,\u001b[Csubqueries,             \u001b[C        \u001b[C         \u001b[130C                                 \r\n triggers, user-defined types and\u001b[Cfunctions,\u001b[Couter joins, multiversion                                                                \r\n concurrency control.\u001b[2CGraphical user interfaces\u001b[Cand\u001b[Cbindings\u001b[Cfor many                                                                \u001b[90C                                           \r\n programming languages\u001b[Care available as\u001b[Cwell.                      \u001b[167C                                 \r\n   \u001b[C  \u001b[C             \u001b[C \u001b[C  \u001b[C      \u001b[C \u001b[C    \u001b[C    \u001b[190C                                 \r\n\u001b[33mN: \u001b[39mThere is 1 additional\u001b[Crecord. Please use the\u001b[C'-a'\u001b[Cswitch to\u001b[Csee\u001b[Cit                                                                 \u001b[92C                                         \u001b[64;8H\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\u001b[13C\u001b[32m❯\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32mwhich\u001b[39m psql      \u001b[6C                                                                                                                                                                                             \u001b[38;2;80;200;120m  /tmp/tmux-1000/default,7127,42\u001b[C\u001b[39m \u001b[65;1H/usr/bin/psql                                                       \